From 91df505ac3eb51afa192e4f8ab654d52f7a356df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 05:53:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): hold an undeclared post script to the lathe door
 on a lathe or mill-turn

A user's own turning script with no `capabilities` line was read as a
mill post, so the #1190 door did not fire and a milling pass could post
with the work spindle at the cutter's rpm. `post::dialect::declared_turning`
now tells "declared not turning" from "undeclared", and
`lathe_voice::at_post` holds an undeclared script to the door for every
operation whose setup mounts a machine with a work spindle (lathe,
mill-turn), naming the missing manifest line and the fix. Declared
scripts and every other machine behave as before; no shipped post or
golden changes.

Fixes #1199

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
